  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SGI-1776 may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target relationships, all of which are mediated by P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1. This protein acts as a bridge, with SGI-1776 directly targeting P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C in multiple pathways. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.5722) indicate a strong, reliable relationship, likely due to the shared biological role of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1 in signaling and enzyme regulation. The presence of multiple distinct compounds—3,3-Diethoxy-1-propanol, hexacosyl (E)-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)prop-2-enoate, and Retrojusticidin B—each targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C further supports the involvement of this enzyme in downstream cellular processes. The evidence suggests that SGI-1776 may modulate Phosphodiesterase 6C activity through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially influencing cellular signaling and function."
